% corpus.trees — a toy 'treebank' for coverage analysis (use with extensional.lex)
c01: [S Rex [VP barks]]
c02: [S [DP every dog] [VP chased [DP a cat]]]
c03: [S [DP the [NP gray cat]] [VP sleeps]]
c04: [S [DP no student] [VP read [DP the book]]]
c05: [S Ann [VP recommended [DP every book]]]
c06: [S [DP most professors] [VP left]]
c07: [S [DP the [NP student [CP who [1 [S t_1 [VP read [DP two books]]]]]]] [VP left]]
c08: [S Rex [VP barks [AdvP loudly]]]
c09: [S Ann [VP gave Bo [DP a book]]]
c10: [S [DP every] [VP barks]]
c11: [S [DP the [NP dog [PP in [DP the garden]]]] [VP barks]]
c12: [S Bo [VP saw [DP a [NP student [PP from [DP every country]]]]]]
c13: [S [DP the cat] [VP is [DP a dog]]]
c14: [S [DP each dog] [VP barks]]
c15: [S Ann [VP is [AP taller [PP than Bo]]]]
c16: [S [DP Rex and Felix] [VP [VP bark] or [VP left]]]
c17: [S Felix [VP chased [DP the mouse]]]
c18: [S [DP every student] [VP [VP read [DP a book]] [AdvP yesterday]]]
